      "sourceLanguage": "en",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 3.21,
          "en": "(gentle music)",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.21,
          "end": 4.56,
          "en": "-: So what is JWT?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.56,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "So JWT stands for JSON Web Token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 11.19,
          "en": "It's a open industry standard with RFC 7519,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.19,
          "end": 14.07,
          "en": "and basically it is a way to transfer data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 14.07,
          "end": 16.74,
          "en": "between two different parties, and that to securely.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.74,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "Okay, now how it looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 22.05,
          "en": "See, whenever you send a token from a server to client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.05,
          "end": 23.73,
          "en": "it can be a normal XML as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.73,
          "end": 26.79,
          "en": "so if you talk about technical world, not the coffee card.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.79,
          "end": 28.17,
          "en": "So let's say if in the technical world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.17,
          "end": 33.06,
          "en": "you will be having this token a JSON data or XML data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 33.06,
          "end": 36.42,
          "en": "but in XML, the length of the data will be lengthy, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.42,
          "end": 38.82,
          "en": "Even for the small amount of data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.82,
          "end": 41.04,
          "en": "you'll be having multiple tags and stuff,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.04,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "plus encrypting it will be a different task.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.02,
          "en": "The other way is you can use normal JSON,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.02,
          "end": 47.76,
          "en": "but again, JSON will be lengthy as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.76,
          "end": 50.52,
          "en": "In that case, we can use some encoded format,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 50.52,
          "end": 53.52,
          "en": "and that's where the JSON web token comes to the picture.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 53.52,
          "end": 55.41,
          "en": "Now this is the format I'm talking about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 55.41,
          "end": 57.15,
          "en": "So when you get a token from the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 57.15,
          "end": 58.62,
          "en": "this is what you will get.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 58.62,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "So this is alphanumeric values, but we can't read it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 64.68,
          "en": "because this is in the encoded format.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 64.68,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "So you can also decode this, and when you decode it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 69.21000000000001,
          "en": "you can see we have three sections here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 69.21000000000001,
          "end": 70.565,
          "en": "Now, before that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 70.565,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "you can see there's a section of algorithms.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 75.24,
          "en": "So by the way, where I am now, I'm on jwt.io,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 75.24,
          "end": 77.73,
          "en": "and you can see we can use different algorithms here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 77.73,
          "end": 79.28999999999999,
          "en": "Remember when I talked about the signature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 79.28999999999999,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "or the encryption?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 83.1,
          "en": "Basically we can use different algorithms here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 83.1,
          "end": 83.97,
          "en": "We have different options.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 83.97,
          "end": 88.5,
          "en": "We got Hs, we got Rs, we got Es, and Ps.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 88.5,
          "end": 90,
          "en": "Now basically we have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 90,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "remember when we talked about the asymmetric and symmetric?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "So basically we have Hs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 98.13,
          "en": "which is HMAC SHA-256, which is symmetric.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 98.13,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "If you want to use asymmetric, we can also use Rs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.07,
          "en": "and higher this numbers, it is better,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 104.07,
          "end": 105.66,
          "en": "because you'll be having a bigger key.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 105.66,
          "end": 107.64,
          "en": "Now here you can see we have three sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 107.64,
          "end": 109.65,
          "en": "So each token will have three sections.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 109.65,
          "end": 111.63,
          "en": "One is the header, one is a payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 111.63,
          "end": 113.28,
          "en": "and next is the signature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 113.28,
          "end": 115.14,
          "en": "Now payload is very important here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 115.14,
          "end": 116.82,
          "en": "because this is where you send your data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 116.82,
          "end": 119.88,
          "en": "So when you say a server's giving some token to the client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 119.88,
          "end": 121.11,
          "en": "with the information,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 121.11,
          "end": 123.9,
          "en": "that information stays inside the payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 123.9,
          "end": 126.66,
          "en": "Example, we got, who is subject the person?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 126.66,
          "end": 128.43,
          "en": "So this is a subject,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 128.43,
          "end": 131.61,
          "en": "a name, this, and the issuance time is this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 131.61,
          "end": 134.46,
          "en": "We can also set the expire time here if you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 134.46,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "You can give a comma and you can say expiry,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.93,
          "en": "and you can give a colon, and you can mention whatever time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 141.93,
          "end": 144.03,
          "en": "So maybe I want to use this time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 145.02,
          "en": "plus I want to change,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 145.02,
          "end": 148.44,
          "en": "let's say I want to make this as 41.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 148.44,
          "end": 149.91,
          "en": "So this is my expiration time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 149.91,
          "end": 152.31,
          "en": "and this should result some values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 152.31,
          "end": 153.45,
          "en": "So issuance is this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 153.45,
          "end": 155.57999999999998,
          "en": "This is a date for today, not today.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 155.57999999999998,
          "end": 159.93,
          "en": "This is a date which is Jan 18th, 2018,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 159.93,
          "end": 162.24,
          "en": "and 7:00 AM, looks like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 162.24,
          "end": 166.05,
          "en": "And if you look here, this is 7:30.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 166.05,
          "end": 168.75,
          "en": "So we got this for 30 minutes, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 168.75,
          "end": 169.583,
          "en": "The token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 169.583,
          "end": 170.64,
          "en": "Of course, the token will expire.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 170.64,
          "end": 172.38,
          "en": "You can set the expire time here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 172.38,
          "end": 174.99,
          "en": "So this is your payload and you can send multiple data here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 174.99,
          "end": 176.7,
          "en": "It's not just you have to send only this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 176.7,
          "end": 177.9,
          "en": "We can add more data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 177.9,
          "end": 182.04,
          "en": "but trying to make payload as small as possible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 182.04,
          "end": 183.69,
          "en": "because you'll be sending this in the header,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 183.69,
          "end": 184.77,
          "en": "and then there are some servers",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 184.77,
          "end": 188.16,
          "en": "which will not accept a bigger chunk of header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 188.16,
          "end": 191.01,
          "en": "So make sure that you don't put unnecessary stuff here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 191.01,
          "end": 192.69,
          "en": "Okay, now this is algorithm which we are using here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 192.69,
          "end": 194.07,
          "en": "which is HS226.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 194.07,
          "end": 195.81,
          "en": "This is what you'll be having in the header.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 195.81,
          "end": 197.43,
          "en": "You can change it and you can use some other algorithm.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 197.43,
          "end": 200.04,
          "en": "Let's say if I want to use R, I can use that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 200.04,
          "end": 201.72,
          "en": "but let me stick to Hs here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 201.72,
          "end": 205.07999999999998,
          "en": "and then we are specifying the type of token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 205.07999999999998,
          "end": 207.06,
          "en": "which is JWT in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 207.06,
          "end": 208.14,
          "en": "Next we have a signature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 208.14,
          "end": 210.42000000000002,
          "en": "So when you say you want to sign it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 210.42000000000002,
          "end": 211.8,
          "en": "you have to use some signature,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 211.8,
          "end": 214.052,
          "en": "and of course, you can use RSA",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 214.052,
          "end": 214.885,
          "en": "where you get two different signatures,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 214.885,
          "end": 216.21,
          "en": "for private and public key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 216.21,
          "end": 217.26,
          "en": "but when you're using Hs,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 217.26,
          "end": 218.55,
          "en": "you'll get only one secret key",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 218.55,
          "end": 221.43,
          "en": "which will be shared by client and server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 221.43,
          "end": 223.16,
          "en": "and you can encrypt it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 223.16,
          "end": 225.36,
          "en": "The problem is when you say encryption,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 225.36,
          "end": 228.03,
          "en": "we are not achieving the actual encryption here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 228.03,
          "end": 228.863,
          "en": "We are just saying",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 228.863,
          "end": 232.32,
          "en": "that no one should be able to modify this token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 232.32,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "So example, if I got a token from the server,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.32999999999998,
          "en": "no one else can hack my token and modify it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 237.32999999999998,
          "end": 238.62,
          "en": "because it is signed, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 238.62,
          "end": 240.72,
          "en": "But what if you want to encrypt it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 240.72,
          "end": 244.2,
          "en": "So we also have an option of encrypting your JWT,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 244.2,
          "end": 246.12,
          "en": "and by the default, we are not doing it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 246.12,
          "end": 248.43,
          "en": "but we can encrypt it, and that's where.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 248.43,
          "end": 251.67,
          "en": "When you are not encrypting your token,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 251.67,
          "end": 253.86,
          "en": "that means anyone can see that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 253.86,
          "end": 255.63,
          "en": "That's right, anyone can see your data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 255.63,
          "end": 259.26,
          "en": "and that's why don't put secret data on in the payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 259.26,
          "end": 262.5,
          "en": "Don't put your phone number or your Social Security number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 262.5,
          "end": 264.21,
          "en": "or your bank password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 264.21,
          "end": 266.52,
          "en": "It should be only these details.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 266.52,
          "end": 268.29,
          "en": "So that's basically JWT.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 268.29,
          "end": 270,
          "en": "Now how we are going to implement this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 270,
          "end": 272.31,
          "en": "So if you want to implement this in your application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 272.31,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "so let's say we are going to build a very simple one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 277.83,
          "en": "where a user sends a request to the server by saying,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 279.21,
          "en": "I want to say hi,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 279.21,
          "end": 280.95,
          "en": "and the server will say, \"Welcome to Telusko.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 280.95,
          "end": 283.71,
          "en": "That's it, a simple API, and I want to secure it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 283.71,
          "end": 284.97,
          "en": "Now how we are gonna do this?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 284.97,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "First step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 286.08,
          "end": 289.89,
          "en": "a client will send the username and password to the server.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 289.89,
          "end": 291.037,
          "en": "A server will say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 291.037,
          "end": 292.74,
          "en": "\"Okay, I'm verifying the username and password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 292.74,
          "end": 295.2,
          "en": "which is correct, and now you are logged in.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 295.2,
          "end": 296.85,
          "en": "Now once you are logged in,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 296.85,
          "end": 300.06,
          "en": "the server will send a JWT token.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 300.06,
          "end": 302.19,
          "en": "Now this token goes to the client,",
